---
source: crates/zdk-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&root.stdout)"
---
Zendesk CLI for AI agents and support operations.

stdout carries data only (plain JSON when piped, tables on a terminal); every
diagnostic goes to stderr; exit codes are stable (see `zdk --help-json`).

  0 ok   1 error   2 usage   3 auth   4 forbidden   5 not found   6 validation
  7 rate limited   9 server   10 config   11 network   12 pagination limit   130 interrupted

Usage: zdk [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  config       Manage the config file and profiles
  completions  Generate shell completions (bash, zsh, fish, powershell, elvish)
  man          Write man pages (zdk.1 and one per subcommand) into a directory
  version      Print version information
  auth         Log in and manage OAuth / API-token credentials
  tickets      Tickets: list, get, show, create, update, reply, assign, solve, delete
  comments     Ticket comments: list, count, make private, redact
  users        Users and end users
  orgs         Organizations
  search       Search tickets, users and organizations
  api          Raw API escape hatch: any method and path, plus the operation registry
  doctor       Check auth, connectivity, rate limits and local configuration

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>
          Profile (Zendesk instance) to target
          
          [env: ZENDESK_PROFILE=]

      --subdomain <SUB>
          Override the subdomain for this call (the `acme` in acme.zendesk.com)

  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          Output format (default: table on a terminal, json when piped)
          
          [possible values: table, json, ndjson, csv, tsv, yaml, raw]

      --fields <A,B,C>
          Keep only these fields (dot paths, comma-separated), e.g. id,subject,assignee.name

      --exclude <A,B>
          Drop these fields (dot paths, comma-separated)

      --compact
          Single-line JSON

      --jq <EXPR>
          Post-process with an embedded jq-compatible filter

      --all
          Auto-paginate to completion

      --limit <N>
          Stop after N records

      --page-size <N>
          Records per page (1-100)

      --sideload <A,B>
          Request sideloads, e.g. users,groups,comment_count

      --dry-run
          Print the request that would be sent and consume no quota

  -y, --yes
          Skip destructive-action confirmation

      --idempotency-key <KEY>
          Explicit Idempotency-Key for writes (auto-generated by default)

      --rate-limit-strategy <STRATEGY>
          What to do when a rate-limit budget is exhausted

          Possible values:
          - wait:  Sleep until the budget refills (default)
          - fail:  Exit 7 as soon as a budget is exhausted
          - burst: Skip the local governor; rely on 429 handling

      --max-concurrency <N>
          In-flight request ceiling

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-request timeout in seconds

      --retries <N>
          Maximum attempts per request (overrides [retry].max_attempts)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-error output on stderr (warnings, progress)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace with redacted request/response logs)

      --no-color
          Disable colour (NO_COLOR is also honoured)

      --audit-log <PATH>
          Append a structured NDJSON record of every API call to this file

      --config <PATH>
          Alternative config file (also ZENDESK_CONFIG)

      --credential-store <STORE>
          Where credentials are kept

          Possible values:
          - auto:    OS keyring when available, else the encrypted file
          - keyring
          - file
          - env:     Read-only: ZENDESK_ACCESS_TOKEN / ZENDESK_EMAIL + ZENDESK_API_TOKEN
          - none:    In-memory only (tests)

      --checkpoint <PATH>
          Write pagination progress to this file and resume from it

Run `zdk config init` to get started, then `zdk auth login`.
